---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const P1 = `MOVE_FORWARD()
MOVE_FORWARD()
ROTATE_RIGHT()
MOVE_FORWARD()`;
const P2 = `REPEAT 3 TIMES
{
  MOVE_FORWARD()
}
ROTATE_LEFT()
MOVE_FORWARD()
MOVE_FORWARD()`;
const P3 = `REPEAT UNTIL(CAN_MOVE(forward))
{
  ROTATE_RIGHT()
}
MOVE_FORWARD()`;
const RefCard = `MOVE_FORWARD()     one square in the direction it faces
ROTATE_LEFT()      turn 90 degrees counterclockwise, in place
ROTATE_RIGHT()     turn 90 degrees clockwise, in place
CAN_MOVE(dir)      true if the next square that way is open
                   dir is left / right / forward / backward
                   RELATIVE TO THE ROBOT, not to the grid

If the robot tries to move into a wall or off the grid, it
stays put and THE PROGRAM ENDS.

IF(condition)      REPEAT n TIMES        REPEAT UNTIL(condition)
{ ... }            { ... }               { ... }
ELSE
{ ... }`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Pseudocode Challenge: Robot on a Grid</h1>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>Objective</h2>

          <p>Three problems on the robot block. This shows up on the exam as a recurring question type with a picture of a grid, and <b>nothing else in this course teaches it</b> &mdash; there is no JavaScript equivalent, so this page is the only place you will meet it before May.</p>

          <p>
            <b>Do this on paper.</b> There is nothing to run and nothing to type.
            On exam day you get this notation on a printed sheet and no
            computer, so practicing it any other way practices the wrong thing.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="reference">
          <h2>Reference Card</h2>

          <p>
            Everything you need for this page. This is the same notation the
            College Board uses on the exam.
          </p>

          <Code
            code={RefCard}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="Exam Notation — what you have so far"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-3">
            <b>Two things catch people every time.</b>{" "}
            <code>DISPLAY</code> puts <b>a space</b> after whatever it shows, so
            two <code>DISPLAY</code> calls in a row give you{" "}
            <code>A B</code> on one line &mdash; not two lines and not{" "}
            <code>AB</code>. And <code>=</code> means <b>equals</b> here, not
            assignment. Assignment is <code>&larr;</code>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="problems">
          <h2>The Problems</h2>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Problem 1 &mdash; trace</h3>

          <p>The robot starts in the bottom-left square of a 4 by 4 grid with every square open, <b>facing up</b>. Where does it end up, and which way is it facing?</p>

          <Code
            code={P1}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="Problem 1"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mb-3"
          />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Problem 2 &mdash; trace</h3>

          <p>Same 4 by 4 grid, all squares open. The robot starts in the bottom-left square <b>facing right</b>.</p>

          <Code
            code={P2}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="Problem 2"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mb-3"
          />

          <p><b>Then answer this:</b> what would happen if the loop said <code>REPEAT 4 TIMES</code> instead? Be specific about what the robot does and what happens to the program.</p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Problem 3 &mdash; trace</h3>

          <p>The robot is somewhere on a grid, facing an unknown direction. Explain in two or three sentences what this program does.</p>

          <Code
            code={P3}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="Problem 3"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mb-3"
          />

          <p><b>Then answer this:</b> describe a situation in which this program never finishes.</p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>Your three answers. For Problems 1 and 2, give the robot's final square and the direction it faces.</p>

          <p>
            Worth <b>3 points</b>, graded on completion. Show your working for
            the traces &mdash; a wrong answer with visible reasoning is worth
            more to both of us than a right one with none.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
